# Shell scripts and container files RUN ON LINUX. A CRLF checkout makes the
# shebang `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r`, and the error is
# `/usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory` — which names a program
# nobody wrote and sends you looking for a missing bash.
#
# This happened here: a Python patch script on Windows rewrote entrypoint.sh in
# text mode and silently converted every line ending.
*.sh            text eol=lf
# .mjs too: scripts/migrate.mjs and scripts/seed-superadmin.mjs are run
# inside the Linux API container, not on the machine that edited them.
*.mjs           text eol=lf
Dockerfile*     text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.sql           text eol=lf
entrypoint.sh   text eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.onnx binary
*.task binary
*.wasm binary
